  "answer": "The checks do not all pass. `make build` succeeded, but `make unit` failed, so `make component` never ran. `make` exited with status 2 (`make: *** [unit] Error 1`). The subagent changed no files, and its full output is in `/tmp/confit_run.log`.\n\n**Build:** it succeeded on net9.0 and net10.0. The only warnings were NU1902, because `Scriban.Signed` 7.2.0 has known moderate-severity vulnerabilities.\n\n**Unit tests:** 39 tests fail on each of net9.0 and net10.0, so 78 failures in total. On each framework, 233 of 272 pass. The failures are all in `SemanticMatcherTests` and `ResultMatcherTests`, and they have two causes:\n\n1. **Matcher names not found (about 38 tests per framework).**\n   - These tests throw `System.ArgumentException : Unknown semantic matcher '<name>' for field '<field>'` at `src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs:61`.\n   - The names in the messages are all lowercase, for example:\n     - `'isuuid' for field 'id'`\n     - `'isisodatetime' for field 'createdAt'`\n     - `'lessthan' for field 'age'`\n     - `'isnull' for field 'deletedAt'`\n     - `'isdomainid' for field 'code'`, which is a custom matcher\n   - This covers the `Apply_*` cases in `SemanticMatcherTests` for IsUuid, IsEmail, IsNull, IsNotNull, IsEmpty, IsNotEmpty, HasLength, GreaterThan, LessThan, IsIsoDate and IsIsoDateTime. It also covers the custom-matcher and nested-path cases.\n   - Four tests in `ResultMatcherTests` fail the same way: `MatchResponseBody_SemanticMatcherValid_PassesAndRemovesField`, `MatchResponseBody_SemanticMatcherFails_ReturnedDescriptionNamesField`, `MatchResponseBody_AllThreeMatcherTypes_EachApplied` and `MatchResponseBody_CustomMatcher_PassesForValidValue`.\n   - `Apply_NullExpected_DoesNotThrow` and `MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow` also fail. The log doesn't show their messages, so I haven't confirmed they share this cause.\n   - The subagent's guess is a case-sensitivity mismatch: the matcher name is lowercased before the lookup, but the `BuiltIns` keys may not be. It did not open `BuiltIns`, so this is unverified.\n\n2. **Wrong exception type (1 test per framework).**\n   - `Apply_FieldAbsentFromResponse_ThrowsInvalidOperationException` fails with `Expected a <System.InvalidOperationException> to be thrown, but found <System.ArgumentException>:`.\n   - This follows from cause 1. The unknown-matcher `ArgumentException` is thrown before the code reaches the \"field absent from the response\" check.\n\nSo the component tests are unverified. The unit failures need fixing before `make component` can run.",
